{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjectorContinuity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjectorContinuity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.generic_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.generic_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L248-L260","doc":"On positive real parameters, every point with `q ≠ 1` is generic; so the density hypothesis\nof `isIdempotentElem_projFamily` reduces to density of `{q ≠ 1}`. For a segment of KZ couplings\nfrom `0` to the imaginary coupling `κ₀` (real `q ∈ [1, q₀]`) this is the density of the segment\nminus its endpoint `κ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sep_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sep_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L239-L245","doc":"Positive real parameters satisfy the separation hypothesis, `q = 1` included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_conj","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L228-L236","doc":"If two families agree up to conjugation at a base point `x₀`, so do their projector families\n(the projector is a polynomial in the generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.isIdempotentElem_projFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.isIdempotentElem_projFamily","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L211-L225","doc":"**(gap 3)** The family is idempotent at every point of `S`, including non-generic base points\nsuch as `q = 1`, provided the generic points are dense in `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_projFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_projFamily","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L200-L209","doc":"**(gap 2)** The family is continuous on `S` as soon as the generator matrices are, provided\n`q` is continuous and nonvanishing on `S` and the `q²`-integers `[d]_{q²}`, `|d| ≤ n`, stay\ndistinct there. No genericity is needed: the set may contain `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_eq_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_eq_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L192-L198","doc":"**(gap 2)** At a generic parameter the family *is* the representation evaluated on the\ninverse Wedderburn matrix unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_eq_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily_eq_map","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L187-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projFamily","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L180-L184","doc":"The image under `ρ x` of the JM projector of `T`: a fixed polynomial in the generator matrices\n`ρ x (σ_i)`, defined at every parameter, including where `q x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_jmProjIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_jmProjIn","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L160-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_list_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_list_prod","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L150-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_jmAddIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.intertwine_jmAddIn","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L136-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.isIdempotentElem_of_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.isIdempotentElem_of_closure","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L121-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_injective_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_injective_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L112-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.notRootOfUnity_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.notRootOfUnity_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L106-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_jmProjIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_jmProjIn","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L84-L100","doc":"**The JM projector is continuous** wherever the `q²`-integers `[d]_{q²}`, `|d| ≤ n`, stay\npairwise distinct — in particular across `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_jmAddIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_jmAddIn","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L73-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_qInt2","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L62-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_list_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.continuousOn_list_prod","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjectorContinuity.lean#L46-L53","signatureChunk":0}]}